<title>THAILAND: IFCT signs deal to run ailing Bkk Bank of Commerce.</title>
<headline>IFCT signs deal to run ailing Bkk Bank of Commerce.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand on Wednesday said it has signed a deal to hire the Industrial Finance Corporation of Thailand to run the financially troubled Bangkok Bank of Commerce for seven years.</p>
<p>According to previously-announced terms of the agreement, the Bank of Thailand will provide financial support to help rescue the bank. It will help buy the bank's non-performing assets worth 60 billion baht at 48 billion baht, it said.</p>
</text>
